# Wireframe: App Shell (Desktop/Tablet)

## Purpose & Flow Context

The application shell wraps all authenticated pages. Entry: user authenticates and is redirected to any auth-gated route. Exit: logout or navigation within content area (sidebar links, header triggers). This wireframe covers viewports >768px. Theme variants (App Shell Light/Dark/System) are not separate wireframes — theme changes only visual tokens (CSS custom properties owned by the design-system), not layout structure. This structural wireframe applies identically to all theme states; the ThemeToggle component and DS color tokens handle visual variation.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `nav`, `main`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + sidebar + content container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Sticky bar: hamburger (hidden >768px), search trigger, notification bell with badge, user avatar with menu trigger, theme toggle | `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100` |
| Sidebar | Team selector, nav links (Issues, Projects, Cycles), collapse toggle | `z-index: 200`; transitions between 240px (expanded) and 56px (collapsed) |
| Content | Main page content rendered by router | `overflow-y: auto`; fills remaining space |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Header — global triggers visible at all times
2. Sidebar — primary navigation context
3. Content — page-specific primary task

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [hamburger] [search] [theme-toggle] [bell 3] [avatar]  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Sidebar (240px) ---+  +-- Content (fills remaining) -----+  |
|  |  [Team Name      ▼]  |  |  [h1 Page Title]                |  |
|  |                       |  |                                  |  |
|  |  [icon] Issues    ●   |  |  (Page-specific content)         |  |
|  |  [icon] Projects     |  |                                  |  |
|  |  [icon] Cycles       |  |                                  |  |
|  |                       |  |                                  |  |
|  |  [<< Collapse]        |  |                                  |  |
|  +-----------------------+  +----------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Header container | Header | Sticky at top; persists across page navigations | Never scrolls away |
| Hamburger button | HamburgerButton | Hidden on desktop/tablet (>768px); visible only in responsive spec | — |
| Search trigger | (in Header) | Click opens command palette (out of scope — trigger only) | aria-label="Search" |
| Notification bell | NotificationBadge | Shows unread count badge; click is trigger only (list out of scope) | Capped at "99+" |
| User avatar | (in Header) | Button with aria-haspopup="true"; click opens user menu (out of scope) | Shows initials fallback |
| Theme toggle | ThemeToggle | Cycles light/dark/system; aria-label reflects current mode | Persisted to localStorage |
| Sidebar container | Sidebar | role="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation" | — |
| Team selector | TeamSelector | Dropdown with team list; icon-only when collapsed | Tooltip shows name when collapsed |
| Nav links | NavLink | Issues / Projects / Cycles; aria-current="page" on active | Tooltip with label when collapsed |
| Collapse toggle | SidebarToggle | aria-label="Collapse sidebar" / "Expand sidebar" | State persisted to localStorage |
| Content area | (main) | role="main"; overflow-y: auto; independent scroll | Full height remaining space |

## Data Display

The content area is a pass-through container for page-specific content — no direct data display. The sidebar displays nav link labels as text; team selector shows team name + icon.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Sidebar heading | "Issues", "Projects", "Cycles" | Navigation labels — user language, consistent across app |
| Team selector | Current team name | Human-readable team name, not ID |
| Theme toggle | "Switch to dark/light/system mode" | Reflects available action, not current state |
| Search trigger | "Search" / "Open command palette" | Consistent with keyboard shortcut hint (future) |
| Notifications | "N unread notifications" | Dynamic count in aria-label |

## States

### Populated (Default)

Full layout as described in the ASCII sketch above. Sidebar expanded (240px) on desktop; collapsible on tablet.

### Empty

N/A — the layout shell always renders. Empty applies to page-specific content within the content area (covered in per-page wireframes).

### Loading

Skeleton mirroring the populated layout while the page content loads within the content area. Sidebar and header render immediately (they contain static navigation and global controls).

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [search] [theme-toggle] [bell] [avatar]                |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Sidebar (240px) ---+  +-- Content (fills remaining) -----+  |
|  |  [Team Name      ▼]  |  |  [===== skeleton bar =====]      |  |
|  |                       |  |  [=== skeleton ===]              |  |
|  |  [icon] Issues        |  |  [======== skeleton =========]   |  |
|  |  [icon] Projects      |  |  [=== skeleton ===]              |  |
|  |  [icon] Cycles        |  |                                  |  |
|  |                       |  |                                  |  |
|  |  [<< Collapse]         |  |                                  |  |
|  +-----------------------+  +----------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

The layout shell itself does not have an error state (it renders structural chrome only). Page-level errors display inline within the content area. Sidebar/header remain functional for navigation.

### Success / Confirmation

N/A — layout shell is persistent. Theme switch success is instantaneous visual feedback.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout as described; sidebar starts expanded |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same layout; sidebar defaults to expanded but can be collapsed via toggle. Collapsed sidebar shows icon-only (56px) |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | header role="banner", nav role="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation", main role="main" |
| Heading order | h1 from page content; layout shell has no heading of its own |
| Reading / Focus order | Header → Sidebar → Content (DOM order) |
| Accessible names | Theme toggle, search trigger, notification bell, user avatar, collapse toggle all get aria-label |
| Keyboard operability | Tab between sidebar links and header controls; Enter/Space to activate; Escape closes any open dropdown/overlay |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation on all interactive targets (nav links, toggle buttons, header triggers) |
| Focus not obscured | Sticky header does not overlap focused sidebar elements; z-index ordering ensures sidebar is above content |
| Non-color intent | Active nav link uses accent background + icon fill; collapse toggle uses icon direction change |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*
